      en: "Kakata Forest Refuge is a protected area near Kakata, Liberia, covering 120 km². It serves as a buffer zone for the more remote national parks. The refuge is home to a small population of western gorillas and the rare white-breasted guinea fowl. It functions as a research site for tropical forest regeneration. The refuge also supports livelihoods through sustainable harvesting of rattan and bamboo. Visitor infrastructure includes a nature center and trails.",
